/remote-jobs\/remote-at-office-pioneer-navigation-global-1135665"},{"slug":"remote-technical-grower-driscolls-emea-1135644","id":"1135644","epoch":1785378568,"date":"2026-07-30T02:29:28+00:00","company":"Driscoll's EMEA","company_logo":"","position":"Technical Grower","tags":["technical"],"description":"<ul><li>Home <\/li><li>About<\/li><li>Join the Driscoll's Family<\/li><li>Job<br><br><\/li><\/ul>Loading job details...<br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **DEPENDABLE** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Vijayawada East, ","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-technical-grower-driscolls-emea-1135644","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-technical-grower-driscolls-emea-1135644"},{"slug":"remote-school-crossing-patrol-chapel-road-primary-school-education-authority-northern-ireland-1135772","id":"1135772","epoch":1785375908,"date":"2026-07-30T01:45:08+00:00","company":"Education Authority (Northern Ireland)","company_logo":"","position":"School Crossing Patrol Chapel Road Primary School","tags":["sys admin","exec","finance","scheme","excel","sales","engineer","recruiter","education","ops","customer support","infosec","travel","medical","game dev","c","legal"],"description":"<strong>PERSON SPECIFICATION<br><br><\/strong><strong>NOTES TO JOB APPLICANTS<br><br><\/strong><ul><li> You must clearly demonstrate on your application form under each question, how, and to what extent you meet the required criteria as failure to do so may result in you not being shortlisted. You should clearly demonstrate this for both the essential and desirable criteria, where relevant.<\/li><li> You must demonstrate how you meet the criteria by the closing date for applications, unless the criteria state otherwise.<\/li><li> The stage in the process when the criteria will be measured is outlined in the table below.<\/li><li> Shortlisting will be carried out on the basis of the essential criteria set out in Section 1 below, using the information provided by you on your application form.<\/li><li> Please note that the Selection Panel reserves the right to shortlist only those applicants that it believes most strongly meet the criteria for the role.<\/li><li> In the event of an excessive number of applications, the Selection Panel also reserves the right to apply any desirable criteria as outlined in Section 3 at shortlisting, in which case these will be applied in the order listed. It is important therefore that you also clearly demonstrate on your application form on how you meet any desirable criteria.<br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Section 1 - Essential Criteria<br><br><\/strong>The following are essential criteria which will initially be measured at the shortlisting stage and which <strong>may also be further explored during the interview\/selection stage<\/strong>. You should therefore make it clear on your application form how, and to what extent you meet these criteria. Failure to do so may result in you not being shortlisted.<br><br><strong>Factor Essential Criteria Method Of Assessment Other<br><br><\/strong>Willingness to undertake job related training<br><br>Shortlisting by Application Form<br><br><strong>S<strong>ection 2 - Essential Criteria<br><br><\/strong><\/strong>The following are <strong>additional essential criteria <\/strong>which will be measured during the interview\/selection stage in line with EA\u00e2\u0080\u0099s Game Changing People Model.<br><br><strong>Factor<\/strong> <strong>Essential Criteria<\/strong> <strong>Method of Assessment<\/strong> <strong>Knowledge<br><br><\/strong>Demonstrable knowledge of road safety and traffic awareness<br><br>Interview<br><br>Skills\/<br><br><strong>Abilities<br><br><\/strong>In line with EA\u00e2\u0080\u0099s Game Changing People Model we will look for evidence of\\:<br><br>Excellent interpersonal and communication skills<br><br>Excellent customer service skills<br><br>Ability to use own initiative while following procedures<br><br>Interview<br><br><strong>Values Orientation<br><br><\/strong>Evidence of how your experience and approach to work reflect EA\u00e2\u0080\u0099s ethos and values. You will find information about our Values here.<br><br>Interview<br><br><strong>Section 3 - Desirable Criteria<br><br><\/strong>Some or all of the desirable criteria may be applied by the Selection Panel in order to determine a manageable pool of candidates. Desirable criteria will be applied in the order listed. You should make it clear on your application form how, and to what extent you meet the desirable criteria, as failure to do so may result in you not being shortlisted.<br><br><strong>Factor<\/strong> <strong>Desirable Criteria<\/strong> <strong>Method of Assessment<\/strong> <strong>Experience<br><br><\/strong>Evidence of experience of working with children and\/or the public<br><br>Shortlisting by Application Form<br><br><strong>Our Values<br><br><\/strong>Through the selection process we will also seek evidence that the personal values of candidates align with those of the EA. This will include evidence of commitment to equality and excellence in service delivery. These reflect our aim which is to meet the needs of all our children and young people equally, removing barriers to learning and ensuring equality of access to excellent education services so that every child can develop to his or her full potential.<br><br><strong>DISCLOSURE OF CRIMINAL BACKGROUND<br><br><\/strong>The Safeguarding Vulnerable Groups (Northern Ireland) Order 2007 defines working directly with children or young people or in specified places as \u00e2\u0080\u0098regulated activity\u00e2\u0080\u0099.<br><br>In the event that you are recommended for appointed to a post that involves \u00e2\u0080\u0098regulated activity\u00e2\u0080\u0099, the Education Authority will be required to undertake an Enhanced Disclosure of Criminal Background. <strong>Please note that you WILL be expected to meet the cost of an Enhanced Disclosure Certificate. Details of how to make payment will be sent to you at the pre-employment stage.<br><br><\/strong>Further information can be accessed on www.nidirect.gov.uk\/campaigns\/accessni-criminal-record-checks or www.justice-ni.gov.uk\/articles\/about-accessni<br><br><strong>APPLICANT GUIDANCE NOTES<br><br><\/strong>To view the applicant guidance notes, please click here.<br><br>To learn about the many great benefits of joining the Education Authority, click here.<br><br><strong>The Education Authority is an Equal Opportunities Employer<br><br><\/strong><strong>JOB DESCRIPTION<\/strong> <strong>REPORTS TO:<\/strong> The Transport Officer <strong>JOB PURPOSE<\/strong> To undertake duties concerned with the safe passage of school children across roads to and from school, (for example, control and direction of traffic at crossing areas, operation of hazard warning signs, and identification of any roadside hazards). <strong>MAIN DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES<br><br><\/strong><ul><li> Control the behaviour of children at crossing areas.<\/li><li> Comply with the relevant provisions contained in the Education Authority\u00e2\u0080\u0099s official booklet of \u00e2\u0080\u009cInstructions to School Crossing Patrols\u00e2\u0080\u009d.<\/li><li> Carry out all duties to comply with: (a) The Health and Safety at Work (NI) order 1978; (b) Acts of Parliament, Statutory Instruments and Regulations and other legal requirements; (c) Codes of Practice.<\/li><li> Carry out all duties out in the working conditions normally inherent in the particular job.<\/li><li> Complete all necessary paperwork.<\/li><li> Carry out duties for jobs up to and including those in the same grade, provided such duties are within the competence of the employee. This job description will be subject to review in light of changing circumstances and is not intended to be rigid and inflexible but should be regarded as providing guidelines within which the individual works. Other duties of a similar nature and appropriate to the grade may be assigned from time to time.<br><br><\/li><\/ul>In accordance with Section 75 of the Northern Ireland Act (1998), the post-holder is expected to promote good relations, equality of opportunity and pay due regard for equality legislation at all times.<br><br>To view the summary of terms and conditions for this post, click here.<br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **SUMPTUOUS** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Londonderry, ","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-school-crossing-patrol-chapel-road-primary-school-education-authority-northern-ireland-1135772","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-school-crossing-patrol-chapel-road-primary-school-education-authority-northern-ireland-1135772"},{"slug":"remote-human-resources-specialist-harvey-nash-1135675","id":"1135675","epoch":1785372050,"date":"2026-07-30T00:40:50+00:00","company":"Harvey Nash","company_logo":"","position":"Human Resources Specialist","tags":["testing","education","exec","content writing","marketing","part time","design","technical","coordinator","customer support","travel","microsoft","ops","excel","medical","digital nomad","consulting","supervisor","dev","speech","sys admin","analyst","finance","c","sales","recruiter","product manager","golang","engineer","full time","python","data annotation","linguistics","data science","junior","stats","internship","senior","hr","payroll"],"description":"<p><strong>Harvey Nash USA<\/strong> has been engaged to find a talented <strong>HR Operations Specialist<\/strong> for a leading healthcare organization committed to delivering exceptional employee experiences through operational excellence.<\/p><p><br><\/p><p><strong>Job Title: <\/strong>HR Operations Specialist<\/p><p><strong>Location: <\/strong>Remote (California Residents Only)<\/p><p><strong>Duration: <\/strong>6-Month Contract<\/p><p><br><\/p><p><strong>About the Role<\/strong><\/p><p>We are seeking a detail-oriented and customer-focused <strong>HR Operations Specialist<\/strong> to join a dynamic HR team. This role is responsible for supporting a wide range of HR operations and employee inquiries while ensuring timely, accurate, and high-quality service delivery. The ideal candidate is resourceful, takes ownership of their work, communicates effectively, and thrives in a fast-paced environment.<\/p><p><br><\/p><p><strong>Day-to-Day Responsibilities<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Review HRIS transactional process requests daily and weekly, approving or rejecting transactions based on established HR policies and procedures.<\/li><li>Understand core HR policies and processes to ensure accurate, timely, and compliant transaction processing.<\/li><li>Escalate complex transactional issues and policy-related questions to HR leadership when appropriate.<\/li><li>Manage employee HR cases, calls, and chats involving benefits, compensation, wellness programs, leave of absence, payroll, performance management, and other HR-related inquiries.<\/li><li>Collaborate with cross-functional HR teams including Benefits, Payroll, HR Technology, Compensation, Talent Acquisition, Employee Relations, Retirement, Eligibility, and Corporate Real Estate to resolve employee issues.<\/li><li>Deliver exceptional customer service by managing cases with accuracy, attention to detail, and professionalism while enhancing the employee experience.<\/li><li>Identify trends in employee inquiries and partner with leadership on process improvements or escalations.<\/li><li>Serve as a trusted HR resource while ensuring compliance with organizational policies and service standards.<\/li><\/ul><p><br><\/p><p><strong>Must-Have Skills<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Resourceful and self-sufficient with the ability to work independently and efficiently.<\/li><li>Demonstrates strong ownership, accountability, and a growth mindset by learning quickly and embracing feedback.<\/li><li>Excellent verbal and written communication skills with a customer-first approach.<\/li><li>Strong understanding of HR processes, policies, and employee support functions.<\/li><li>Experience handling HR service requests or HR operations in a shared services or HR support environment.<\/li><\/ul><p><br><\/p><p><strong>Preferred Skills<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Experience with Oracle HCM.<\/li><li>Experience with UKG (Ultipro<strong>)<\/strong> and\/or ServiceNow.<\/li><li>Passion for Human Resources with broad HR knowledge; SHRM-CP certification is a plus.<\/li><li>Strong relationship-building and stakeholder management skills.<\/li><li>Experience supporting multiple HR Centers of Excellence.<\/li><\/ul><p><br><\/p><p><strong>Education<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Associate's or bachelor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s degree in human resources or a related field OR 5+ years of HR experience in lieu of a degree.<\/li><\/ul><p><br><\/p><p>A reasonable, good faith estimate of the minimum and maximum hourly wage for this position is <strong>$25.00 - $29.00 per hour on W2<\/strong>, depending on experience.<\/p><p><br><\/p><p><strong>About Us<\/strong><\/p><p>Harvey Nash is a national, full-service talent management firm specializing in technology and professional staffing. Our company was founded with a mission to serve as the talent partner of choice by connecting exceptional talent with leading organizations across a wide range of industries.<\/p><br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **FASCINATINGLY** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"California, California, United States","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-human-resources-specialist-harvey-nash-1135675","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-human-resources-specialist-harvey-nash-1135675"},{"slug":"remote-construction-project-coordinator-linesteel-1973-limited-1135898","id":"1135898","epoch":1785371571,"date":"2026-07-30T00:32:51+00:00","company":"Linesteel (1973) Limited","company_logo":"","position":"construction project coordinator","tags":["education","customer support","content writing","medical","non tech","hr","infosec","supervisor","marketing","finance","exec","recruiter","full time","travel","sys admin","virtual assistant","technical","dev","golang","digital nomad","ops","math","microsoft","excel","sales","engineer","testing","mobile","c","junior","payroll","embedded","accounting","game dev","speech","ruby","design","transcribing","controller","adult","senior","web dev","teaching","coordinator"],"description":"<strong>Overview<br><br><\/strong>Languages<br><br>English<br><br>Education<br><br><ul><li> No degree, certificate or diploma <br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Experience<br><br><\/strong>1 year to less than 2 years<br><br>On site<br><br>Work must be completed at the physical location. There is no option to work remotely.<br><br><strong>Benefits<br><br><\/strong>Health benefits<br><br><ul><li> Health care plan<\/li><\/ul><br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **DEFT** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Barrie, ","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-construction-project-coordinator-linesteel-1973-limited-1135898","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-construction-project-coordinator-linesteel-1973-limited-1135898"},{"slug":"remote-traveler-care-specialist-luxury-travel-zicasso-1135640","id":"1135640","epoch":1785369604,"date":"2026-07-30T00:00:04+00:00","company":"Zicasso","company_logo":"","position":"Traveler Care Specialist Luxury Travel","tags":["travel","education","transcribing","dev","marketing","exec","video","ops","excel","stats","sales","recruiter","digital nomad"],"description":"<p><\/p><p>Company Overview<\/p><p>Established in 2008, Zicasso is the most-reviewed and highest-rated luxury travel company, specializing in immersive custom tours, vacations, and safaris. Our Zicasso travel specialists are the world\u00e2\u0080\u0099s top 2% of boutique tour operators and travel agents, pre-vetted and handpicked to compete in creating itineraries tailored to each of our travelers\u00e2\u0080\u0099 unique preferences. Joining Zicasso, you'll play a key role in bringing our travelers\u00e2\u0080\u0099 dreams to life\u00e2\u0080\u0094pushing the boundaries of what\u00e2\u0080\u0099s possible with luxury travel experiences.<\/p><p>As a member of our team, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll be part of a company recognized for its strong brand reputation among discerning travelers. Our authority in the luxury travel industry is consistently affirmed through features in top media outlets, including The New York Times, The Wall Street Journal, BBC, Forbes, CNN, and Cond\u00c3\u00a9 Nast Traveler, to name a few. See our press coverage here.<\/p><p>We are a fully remote company spanning five continents, and we foster a dynamic, progressive global work environment that values creativity, initiative, and continuous learning. We're seeking passionate, data-driven individuals who thrive in a high-performance environment and are eager to contribute to our innovative company culture, underpinned by a consistent pursuit of excellence, integrity, and teamwork.<\/p><p>Our global team comes together biannually for international retreats and summits. These are typically held for a week at a new location each time, providing opportunities to share ideas, collaborate in person, and strengthen our culture, all while learning firsthand about the destinations we serve. These events embody our commitment to both professional growth and the transformative power of travel.<\/p><p>Join us in shaping the future of luxury travel while working towards our vision\u00e2\u0080\u0094creating a more connected humanity through travel. To learn more, visit https:\/\/www.zicasso.com\/careers.<\/p><p><\/p><p><\/p><p><\/p><p><br \/>The Role<\/p><p>Currently, we are seeking a highly motivated, customer service-minded Traveler Care Specialist who embraces an entrepreneurial spirit and has a passion for international travel!<\/p><p>This role will be working at the intersection of our travelers and Zicasso\u00e2\u0080\u0099s global network of travel providers (partners), making both sides delighted with Zicasso\u00e2\u0080\u0099s unique matching service and will be responsible for assessing and processing incoming travel inquiries via email\/messaging, phone, and online. You will learn to understand analytics and help ensure that we are maximizing the potential of our leads. You will build trusted relationships with our travelers to understand their travel needs and ensure these needs are being met and their expectations exceeded. This position plays a key role towards driving loyalty and repeat bookings of our most valued travelers.<\/p><p>This is an international, fully remote, freelance contractor position, working from home with a 5-day workweek that includes rotating weekend shifts. Initial training (3 to 4 weeks) will take place Monday through Friday.\u00c2\u00a0<\/p><p>This role is open to candidates located outside of the United States, with a strong preference for those based in Argentina, Costa Rica, Brazil, and Colombia.<\/p><p>The work will all be conducted in English.<\/p><p><\/p><p><\/p><p><br \/>Key Responsibilities<\/p><ul><li>Provide exceptional customer service to travelers by taking ownership of their inquiries and becoming a trusted advisor throughout their use of Zicasso services. This includes assessing and solving incoming traveler inquiries via phone, live chat, messages and email.<\/li><li>Build trusted, long-lasting relationships with discerning luxury clients to strengthen their confidence in Zicasso. This involves assisting and serving clients in a way that meets their needs and exceeds their expectations.<\/li><li>Ensure a high level of inquiry conversion by demonstrating expertise in consultation, product knowledge, and the benefits of using Zicasso. This includes speaking with travelers via phone calls (and sometimes video), helping them understand how Zicasso works, and providing guidance for their travel needs.<\/li><li>Participate cross-functionally with the Partnerships, Product, and Marketing teams to integrate best practices and solutions for the client's experience and\/or issues that may arise.<\/li><li>Partner with the Care Team leadership on projects and initiatives to solve problems and create innovative solutions.<\/li><li>Leverage Zicasso\u00e2\u0080\u0099s data, analytics and technology\u00c2\u00a0 to set new standards for customer success, driving innovation and excellence for the luxury travel industry.<\/li><li>Provide consultation and advice to move general inquiries to destination-specific trip requests.<\/li><li>Coach and mentor team members as needed.<\/li><\/ul><p><\/p><p>Please Note: We\u00e2\u0080\u0099re seeking highly-motivated candidates. Those who excel in this role will be given the opportunity to take on increasingly complex projects and initiatives, and grow their role and responsibility within the Traveler Care Team.<\/p><p><\/p><p><\/p><p><br \/>Required Skills and Experience<\/p><ul><li>Minimum 8+ years of experience in the travel industry, with a focus on travel sales or operations of luxury tours or hotels. Examples of relevant experience include tour leader, tour director, hotel front desk, client relations, or guest services<\/li><li>Passionate about travel, with extensive experience traveling abroad and a strong curiosity about new international destinations.<\/li><li>Strong customer service-focused skills, with a passion for building strong relationships with travelers. This includes being comfortable with telephone-based work as a key part of the role.<\/li><li>Excellent fluency in oral and written English.<\/li><li>A cheerful and confident person who is adaptable to different styles of communication and traveler behaviors.<\/li><li>Highly motivated and enthusiastic, with a willingness to put in extra effort in a start-up environment to drive company success.<\/li><li>Comfortable with technology and able to quickly learn and adapt to the use of new software. Thorough knowledge of Google Workspace (formerly G Suite) (e.g. Docs, Sheets, Slides) is preferred.<\/li><li>Strong organizational skills and attention to detail, striving to achieve quality, error-free work.<\/li><li>Work flexible hours, including weekends, evenings, and holidays.<\/li><li>A Bachelor's degree or higher is preferred.<br \/><br \/><\/li><\/ul><p><br \/>What We Offer:<\/p><ul><li>Remote work from your home base and flexible hours that allow you to enjoy a great work-life balance.<\/li><li>Innovative, fast-paced and collaborative culture that values diverse voices and opinions.<\/li><li>Learning and development annual stipend.<\/li><li>Enjoy two company-sponsored business trips each year at international destinations we serve!<\/li><\/ul><p><\/p><p>If you are a customer service-minded problem solver with a passion for travel and a strong desire to make a difference, we strongly encourage you to apply for this exciting opportunity to join our team and help shape the future of personalized, life-enriching travel experiences at Zicasso!<\/p><p><\/p><p>All applications should be submitted in English.<\/p><p><\/p><p><br \/>Our Commitment to Candidates<\/p><p>Zicasso is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicable to all locations, all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by local law. We provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities; if you need an accommodation to participate in the application process, please contact careers@zicasso.com.<\/p><p><\/p><p>At Zicasso, we value a highly personalized recruitment journey. For recruiting purposes, we may use AI tools to review, transcribe, and record application materials and interviews, but this is always under human review and judgment. All final hiring determinations are made exclusively by our hiring teams.<\/p><p><\/p><br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **PAMPER** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-traveler-care-specialist-luxury-travel-zicasso-1135640","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-traveler-care-specialist-luxury-travel-zicasso-1135640"},{"slug":"remote-project-administrator-bavarian-capital-1135720","id":"1135720","epoch":1785362905,"date":"2026-07-29T22:08:25+00:00","company":"Bavarian Capital","company_logo":"","position":"Project Administrator","tags":["macos","education","speech","content writing","non tech","hr","teaching","exec","design","technical","marketing","travel","payroll","ops","recruiter","full time","digital nomad","customer support","dev","finance","admin","sys admin"],"description":"Bavarian Capital is adding a Project Administrator to support our ongoing coordination efforts for a major engagement with a leading Spanish telecommunications provider. This role ensures that our internal processes remain organized and that project timelines are managed with the precision our partners expect. By focusing on administrative clarity, you help maintain the high standards of documentation and scheduling that define our firm.<br>  <br><strong>About the role<br><\/strong> As a Project Administrator, you will serve as a central point of coordination for the team, handling the logistical and administrative tasks that keep our projects moving forward. You will work closely with project leads to track progress, update documentation, and facilitate clear communication across different workstreams. This is an entry level position designed for someone who is highly organized and wants to start a career in project management within a professional investment firm. The role is fully remote, requiring a professional who can manage their tasks independently while staying connected with a distributed team.<br>  <br><strong>What you will do<\/strong><ul> <li>Maintain and update project schedules to ensure all milestones are recorded and visible to the team.<\/li> <li>Organize and manage digital files and documentation related to the Spanish telecommunications engagement.<\/li> <li>Prepare regular status reports that summarize project progress for internal reviews and meetings.<\/li> <li>Coordinate internal meetings and ensure that all participants have the necessary materials and agendas beforehand.<\/li> <li>Track project expenses and administrative tasks to assist with budget oversight and record keeping.<\/li> <li>Assist with the drafting of internal updates to keep all team members informed of project developments.<\/li> <li>Monitor project timelines to identify any potential delays early in the process and report them to leads.<\/li> <li>Update internal databases and project management tools to reflect the most current information.<\/li> <br><br><\/ul><strong>What we are looking for<\/strong><ul> <li>A background in business administration, management, or a related field of study.<\/li> <li>Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple administrative tasks simultaneously.<\/li> <li>Clear and professional written and verbal communication abilities.<\/li> <li>Basic familiarity with standard project management tools and documentation software.<\/li> <li>A methodical approach to work with a high level of attention to detail and accuracy.<\/li> <li>The ability to work effectively and independently in a fully remote environment.<\/li> <li>A reliable and professional attitude toward meeting deadlines and following internal instructions.<\/li> <li>Proficiency in standard office applications for documentation, data entry, and scheduling.<\/li> <br><br><\/ul><strong>What we offer<\/strong><ul> <li>A permanent, full-time position within a stable and respected investment firm.<\/li> <li>A fully remote working arrangement that supports professional autonomy and focus.<\/li> <li>Competitive pay that reflects the responsibilities of the role and the current market.<\/li> <li>Opportunities for professional development and learning within the project management field.<\/li> <li>A professional home where your contributions to project efficiency are recognized.<\/li> <li>Access to modern tools and systems that support reliable remote collaboration.<\/li> <li>A calm and focused working environment free from the distractions of a traditional office.<\/li> <li>The chance to work on large scale projects with significant international partners.<\/li> <br><br><\/ul><strong>Working at Bavarian Capital<br><\/strong> Bavarian Capital is built on a foundation of reliability and long term thinking. We avoid the frantic pace often found in the investment sector, preferring instead to move with purpose and precision. This approach extends to how we manage our team, offering a high degree of professional autonomy and a clear, remote first structure. We believe that by providing a stable and respectful environment, our team members can focus on their craft and produce their best work. This role is a chance to start a career in an organization that values clarity, thoughtful decision making, and the sustainable growth of its people and its projects. We prioritize steady progress over short term trends, ensuring that every member of our team has a reliable and predictable path forward.<br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **INTERESTS** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Valencia\/Val\u00c3\u00a8ncia, Valencia\/Val\u00c3\u00a8ncia, Comunidad Valenciana \/ Comunitat Valenciana, Espa\u00c3\u00b1a","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-project-administrator-bavarian-capital-1135720","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-project-administrator-bavarian-capital-1135720"},{"slug":"remote-software-engineer-go-wakacje-pl-1135634","id":"1135634","epoch":1785355201,"date":"2026-07-29T20:00:01+00:00","company":"Wakacje.pl","company_logo":"","position":"Software Engineer GO","tags":["golang","dev","travel","api","golang","engineer","backend","digital nomad"],"description":"Remote - Market-leading travel agency (part of an international holding) working with numerous tour operator partners  is looking for a Golang Developers to join our core backend engineering team. Our developers focus heavily on building robust API integrations between our inter...<br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **HEARTFELT** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-software-engineer-go-wakacje-pl-1135634","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-software-engineer-go-wakacje-pl-1135634"},{"slug":"remote-copy-editor-missionstaff-1135668","id":"1135668","epoch":1785352022,"date":"2026-07-29T19:07:02+00:00","company":"MissionStaff","company_logo":"","position":"Copy Editor","tags":["testing","education","exec","content writing","marketing","part time"],"description":"<p>We connect top talent in Business Services, Tech, Marketing &amp; Creative with companies of all sizes\u00e2\u0080\u0094offering flexible, high-touch staffing solutions. We are currently filling the following contract job for our client.<\/p><p><strong>Job Title<\/strong>: Copy Editor<br><br>  *30 hours\/week<br><br>  *6 month contract with likely extensions<\/p><p><strong>Overview<\/strong>:<br><br>  Join a dynamic content development team as a Copy Editor, responsible for ensuring the accuracy, clarity, and quality of test item content. This part-time role is pivotal in supporting product maintenance and new production, contributing to high standards of content delivery. If you are detail-oriented with a passion for precision and excellence, this position offers a unique opportunity to make an impact in educational content.<\/p><p><strong>Required Skills<\/strong>:<\/p><ul><li>Proven experience as a copy editor, preferably in educational or exam content<\/li><li>Exceptional attention to detail and strong proofreading skills<\/li><li>Excellent command of grammar, punctuation, and style guides<\/li><li>Ability to work independently and meet tight deadlines<\/li><li>Strong organizational and time management skills<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Nice to Have Skills<\/strong>:<\/p><ul><li>Experience with standardized testing or assessment development<\/li><li>Familiarity with content management systems and editing tools<\/li><li>Prior experience working on certification or exam content<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Preferred Education and Experience<\/strong>:<\/p><ul><li>Bachelor's degree in English, Communications, Education, or a related field<\/li><li>2+ years of editing experience in a professional environment<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Other Requirements<\/strong>:<\/p><ul><li>Part-time commitment of up to 30 hours per week<\/li><li>Comfortable working remotely or on-site as required<\/li><li>Ability to produce a high volume of content reliably within project timelines<\/li><\/ul><p>If you are ready to contribute your expertise to a vital project and thrive in a collaborative environment, we encourage you to apply now and join a team dedicated to excellence.<\/p><p>MissionStaff is an equal opportunity employer. Please note that we do not accept unsolicited resumes from third-party recruiters or agencies. Additionally, candidates must be U.S. citizens or Permanent Residents to be considered for this position.<br><\/p><br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **CALM** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Pennsylvania, Pennsylvania, United States","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-copy-editor-missionstaff-1135668","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-copy-editor-missionstaff-1135668"},{"slug":"remote-ecology-and-society-section-on-emergency-and-crisis-management-secm-1135655","id":"1135655","epoch":1785350281,"date":"2026-07-29T18:38:01+00:00","company":"Section on Emergency and Crisis Management (SECM)","company_logo":"","position":"Ecology and Society","tags":["education","technical","customer support","exec","ops","supervisor","sys admin","medical","infosec","web dev","c","pascal","mobile","content writing"],"description":"Skip to content<br><br>Opens in a new window Opens an external site Opens an external site in a new window<br><br><ul><li>Current Issue<\/li><li>About the Journal<\/li><ul><li>Our Editors<\/li><li>Policies<\/li><li>Submissions<\/li><li>Contact<\/li><\/ul><li>Open Access Policy<\/li><li>Submit an Article<\/li><li>Sign In<br><\/li><\/ul>Icons\/Search<br><br>Icons\/Close<br><br>Icons\/Search<br><br>A journal of integrative science<br><br>for resilience and sustainability<br><br>Issue selector block \u00e2\u0080\u0093 please see right sidebar for options.<br><br>Volume 31, Issue 3July 2026<br><br>Table of Contents List of Special Features Past Issues<br><br>Article selector block \u00e2\u0080\u0093 please see right sidebar for options.<br><br>Adaptive capacity of fishing companies facing spatial competition with offshore wind farms: insights from scallop fishers in Normandy (France)<br><br>H\u00c3\u00a9l\u00c3\u00a8ne Buchholzer, C\u00c3\u00a9lya Martial, Marjolaine Fr\u00c3\u00a9sard, Pascal Le Floc\u00e2\u0080\u0099h<br><br>Weaving relational values around a threatened river landscape: bundles, interrelations, and social drivers from northern Chile<br><br>Matilde Larraechea, Mat\u00c3\u00adas Guerrero-Gatica, I\u00c3\u00b1igo Bidegain, Claudia Cerda<br><br>Au