anuel Ebner<br><br>Technical University of Munich, Ecosystem Dynamics and Forest Management Group, TUM School of Life Sciences; Bechtesgaden National Park; Universit\u00c3\u00a4t Innsbruck, Department of Ecology<br><br>Marjolaine Fr\u00c3\u00a9sard<br><br>Universit\u00c3\u00a9 de Bretagne Occidentale, UMR AMURE, Plouzan\u00c3\u00a9, France<br><br>Mat\u00c3\u00adas Guerrero-Gatica<br><br>Facultad de Ciencias Forestales y de la Conservaci\u00c3\u00b3n de la Naturaleza, Universidad de Chile; Instituto de Ecolog\u00c3\u00ada y Biodiversidad (IEB), Santiago, Chile; Grupo de Investigaci\u00c3\u00b3n Ecolog\u00c3\u00ada Naturaleza y Sociedad (ECONAS), Santiago, Chile<br><br>Matilde Larraechea<br><br>Grupo de Investigaci\u00c3\u00b3n Ecolog\u00c3\u00ada Naturaleza y Sociedad (ECONAS), Santiago, Chile<br><br>Pascal Le Floc\u00e2\u0080\u0099h<br><br>Universit\u00c3\u00a9 de Bretagne Occidentale, UMR AMURE, Plouzan\u00c3\u00a9, France<br><br>Ricardo Safra de Campos<br><br>University of Exeter, Exeter, UK<br><br>Tara Quinn<br><br>United Kingdom Health Security Agency London, UK<br><br>Ulrike Tappeiner<br><br>Universit\u00c3\u00a4t Innsbruck, Department of Ecology; Institute for Alpine Environment, Eurac Research<br><br>Submit an Article<br><br>This journal provides open access to all of its content on the principle that making research freely available to the public supports a greater global exchange of knowledge.<br><br>Sign in and Submit<br><br>Submission Guidelines<br><br>Special Features selector block \u00e2\u0080\u0093 please see right sidebar for options.<br><br>Special Features<br><br>Enhancing Social-Ecological Resilience and Equity in Southern Africa: insights from Research and Practice<br><br>Feature-in-Progress<br><br>Seeds of Good Anthropocenes: Envisioning and Exploring Pathways toward Transformative Futures<br><br>Feature-in-Progress<br><br>Beyond the Assessment on the Diverse Values of Nature: Hidden gems, Biases, Frontiers, Challenges, and Insights<br><br>Feature-in-Progress<br><br>The Coproduction of Conflicts in Environmental Sustainability: Concepts, Methods, and Ethics<br><br>Feature-in-Progress<br><br>State-Reinforced Transformative and Adaptive Governance of Sustainable Social-Ecological Systems<br><br>Feature-in-Progress<br><br>Submit a Special Feature Proposal<br><br>Learn More<br><br>See all Special Features<br><br>Featured Topic block \u00e2\u0080\u0093 please see right sidebar for options.<br><br>Featured topic<br><br>Anthropocene<br><br>01\/2026<br><br>Seeding equity in African food systems: how can marginal, bottom-up initiatives promote transformations to more equitable and sustainable futures?<br><br>Julia L. van Velden, Nyasha Magadzire, Willem Malherbe, Joyce Atieno Ojino, Helen Bour, Keziah K. Mayer, Sungeni R. Karonga, S\u00c3\u00a8nankpon Tcheton, Mulako Kabisa, Laura M. Pereira, Reinette Biggs<br><br>05\/2025<br><br>Pathways to transformation: institutionalizing urban agriculture in a Montr\u00c3\u00a9al borough<br><br>Olivia St-Laurent, Karina Benessaiah, Elena M. Bennett<br><br>03\/2025<br><br>The seeds\u00e2\u0080\u0099 substrate: a concept to understand how transformations toward Good Anthropocenes can be enabled<br><br>Ignacio Gianelli, Micaela Trimble, Silvana Juri, Laura M. Pereira, Blanca Gonz\u00c3\u00a1lez-Mon, Sebasti\u00c3\u00a1n Villasante<br><br>Authorship Map \u00e2\u0080\u0093 please see right sidebar for options.<br><br>Around the world<br><br>Authorship<br><br>These are the top ten countries that our authors from the last twelve months have been from.<br><br><ul><li>United States<\/li><li>Netherlands<\/li><li>Canada<\/li><li>Germany<\/li><li>South Africa<\/li><li>Sweden<\/li><li>Spain<\/li><li>Australia<\/li><li>Mexico<\/li><li>Chile<br><br><\/li><\/ul>Journal metrics and most viewed articles in this issue<br><br>141<br><br>H Index<br><br>4.403<br><br>ISI 2021 Impact Factor<br><br>5.275<br><br>5 Year Impact Factor<br><br>Article selector block \u00e2\u0080\u0093 please see right side