iversity policy<br><br>Dolly J\u00c3\u00b8rgensen<br><br>Special Feature Ecological Restoration, Ecosystem Services, and Land Use<br><br>12\/2015<br><br>Theories of the deep: combining salience and network analyses to produce mental model visualizations of a coastal British Columbia food web<br><br>Jordan Levine, Michael Muthukrishna, Kai M.A. Chan, Terre Satterfield<br><br>Subscribe for updates<br><br><ul><li> indicates required<br><br><\/li><\/ul>First Name *<br><br>Last Name *<br><br>Email Address *<br><br><ul><li>Submit an Article<\/li><li>Submission Guidelines<\/li><li>Current Issue<\/li><li>Journal Policies<\/li><li>Find Back Issues<\/li><li>Open Access Policy<\/li><li>Find Features<\/li><li>Contact<br><br><\/li><\/ul>Resilience Alliance is a registered 501 (c)(3) non-profit organization<br><br>Permissions and Copyright Information<br><br>Online and Open Access since 1997<br><br>Ecology and Society is now licensing all its articles under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License<br><br>Ecology and Society ISSN: 1708-3087<br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **INEXPENSIVE** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Society, ","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-ecology-and-society-section-on-emergency-and-crisis-management-secm-1135655","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-ecology-and-society-section-on-emergency-and-crisis-management-secm-1135655"},{"slug":"remote-postuler-chez-nous-jubin-freres-1135632","id":"1135632","epoch":1785350063,"date":"2026-07-29T18:34:23+00:00","company":"Jubin Fr\u00c3\u00a8res","company_logo":"","position":"Postuler chez nous","tags":["infosec","javascript","exec","recruiter","c"],"description":"Formulaire de postulation<br><br>Remplissez le formulaire ci-dessous afin de nous faire part de votre postulation et CV<br><br>Compl\u00c3\u00a9ter 0%<br><br>1 Vos coordonn\u00c3\u00a9es 2 Postulation<br><br>Poste *<br><br>Pr\u00c3\u00a9nom *<br><br>Nom *<br><br>Adresse<br><br>NPA<br><br>Localit\u00c3\u00a9<br><br>T\u00c3\u00a9l\u00c3\u00a9phone *<br><br>Adresse courriel *<br><br>Pr\u00c3\u00a9c\u00c3\u00a9dent Suivant<br><br>Compl\u00c3\u00a9ter 50%<br><br>1 Vos coordonn\u00c3\u00a9es 2 Postulation<br><br>Type de poste *<br><br>Select Bureau Shop Autre<br><br>Votre dossier de candidature *Maximum 10Mo<br><br>Glisser-d\u00c3\u00a9poser des fichiers ici Parcourir les Fichiers<br><br>Message *<br><br>Envoyer<br><br>Pr\u00c3\u00a9c\u00c3\u00a9dent Suivant<br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **RECTIFYING** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Chez Nous, ","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-postuler-chez-nous-jubin-freres-1135632","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-postuler-chez-nous-jubin-freres-1135632"},{"slug":"remote-hr-generalist-1-talent-software-services-1135696","id":"1135696","epoch":1785348386,"date":"2026-07-29T18:06:26+00:00","company":"TALENT Software Services","company_logo":"","position":"HR Generalist 1","tags":["design","music","customer support","travel","video","exec","content writing","ops","marketing","ads","digital nomad","hr","dev","consulting","technical","testing","payroll","education"],"description":"Day to Day Responsibilities<br><br>(Being thorough in this section will allow the suppliers to pre-identify candidates more accurately.)<br><br><ul><li>Review all HRIS transactional process requirements on a daily\/weekly and as needed basis and manages the approval or rejection process<\/li><li>Understand the core HR policies and processes to make quality and timely processing decisions<\/li><li>Escalate transactional process issues and advanced issues to management for review<\/li><li>Manage all incoming HR cases\/calls\/chats requiring significant, HR Generalist knowledge and understanding a wide variety of HR processes, policies, and technical procedures such as questions pertaining to benefits, compensation, wellness programs, and leave of absence<\/li><li>Leverage other key business contacts as needed to resolve employee inquiries and related processes and deliverables (i.e., LOA, Benefits, Retirement, HR Tech, Payroll, Compensation, Employee Relations, Talent Acquisition, Eligibility, Performance Management, Benefits, Corporate Real Estate)<\/li><li>Manage cases with the utmost care, quality, and attention to detail, all while providing accurate information while enhancing the employee's experience with HR:Connect<\/li><li>Consult with leadership on any possible trends or escalations and may become point of contact for reaching out to other HR Centers of Excellence<br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Required Skills (top 3 Non-negotiables)<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Resourceful - self-sufficient (efficient)<\/li><li>Takes ownership - fails fast and learns fast. Coachable\/Receives feedback well and seeks it as well. <\/li><li>Strong Communicator - verbal and written<br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Preferred Skills (nice To Have)<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Oracle HCM experience<\/li><li>Passion for HR. Possesses HR knowledge - extending to SHRM CP<\/li><li>Strong relationship builder<br><br><\/li><\/ul>Disqualifiers\/Dislikes on Resumes<br><br><ul><li>Inexperience with HR and high-volume work environment\/high case load. <br><br><\/li><\/ul>Education Requirements<br><br><ul><li>Associates or Bachelors in HR or 5 years of HR experience in lieu of education<br><br><\/li><\/ul>Required Testing<br><br><ul><li>N\/A<br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Software Skills Required<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Experience in Oracle HCM, Ultipro\/UKG, and\/or ServiceNow Preferred<br><br><\/li><\/ul>Required Certifications<br><br><ul><li>None - HR certifications would be a bonus<\/li><\/ul><br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **PRODIGIOUS** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"California, California, United States","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-hr-generalist-1-talent-software-services-1135696","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-hr-generalist-1-talent-software-services-1135696"},{"slug":"remote-customer-account-associate-albertsons-nestle-1135671","id":"1135671","epoch":1785346000,"date":"2026-07-29T17:26:40+00:00","company":"Nestl\u00c3\u00a9","company_logo":"","position":"Customer Account Associate Albertsons","tags":["testing","education","exec","content writing","marketing","part time","design","technical","coordinator","customer support","travel","microsoft","ops","excel","medical","digital nomad","consulting","supervisor","dev","speech","sys admin","analyst","finance","c","sales","recruiter"],"description":"Foods you love. Brands you trust. And a career that empowers you to grow.<br><br>At Nestl\u00c3\u00a9 USA, we\u00e2\u0080\u0099re all working towards the same goal \u00e2\u0080\u0093 to delight and deliver for our consumers. With a rich portfolio of beloved brands, including DiGiorno, Toll House, and Coffee mate, in 97% of U.S. households, we have a unique opportunity \u00e2\u0080\u0093 and responsibility \u00e2\u0080\u0093 to be there for every moment in our consumers\u00e2\u0080\u0099 lives.<br><br>Joining Nestl\u00c3\u00a9 means becoming part of an inclusive workplace that inspires innovation, encourages strategic thinking and creativity, and celebrates your achievements. No matter where you work within the organization, you are empowered to challenge the status quo, embrace risk-taking, and pioneer new ideas. Our supportive and collaborative environment encourages bold ambitions and continuous learning so that everyone can grow and thrive.<br><br><em>This position is not eligible for Visa Sponsorship.<br><br><\/em><strong>Position Overview:<br><br><\/strong>The Associate, Customer Account is a key member of the Account Management team, supporting Account Directors and Account Managers in achieving annual sales objectives through customer account support, distributor coordination, and systems administration.<br><br><strong>Responsibilities:<br><br><\/strong><strong>Trade Auditing\/Analysis (Deductions, Fines, Claims, Post-Audit Work) <\/strong>(40% of Role)<br><br><ul><li>Support trade deduction analysis, reconciliation, workflow administration, and documentation in partnership with Account Management and Sales Finance.<\/li><li>Manage customer post-audit claims, including undisputed claim resolution, disputed claim tracking, and timely response management.<\/li><li>Research and resolve deduction discrepancies, lead follow-up on complex claims, and participate in customer\/vendor meetings as needed.<\/li><li>Drive collection of unauthorized deductions and credits while supporting profitable business performance.<\/li><li>Support customer metric forecasting, off-invoice trade events, planning tool inputs, and alignment between customer and internal systems.<\/li><li>Reconcile customer forecasts with Nestl\u00c3\u00a9 internal forecasts and support new item setup, trade management, and financial reconciliations.<br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Customer Distributor Support <\/strong>(10% of AA Role)<br><br><ul><li>Coordinate with Nestl\u00c3\u00a9 Retail Services on logistics, distribution activities, NRS workbooks, and sell sheets.<\/li><li>Prepare upcoming-period NRS materials and participate in monthly distributor touchpoints.<\/li><li>Resolve distributor-to-customer system connectivity issues and monitor out-of-stock reporting, sales impact, and follow-up communications.<br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Customer Account Team Support &amp; Systems Administration <\/strong>(50% of AA Role)<br><br><ul><li>Maintain customer forms, item data, product attributes, UPCs, dimensions, pricing information, and customer item management records.<\/li><li>Support item setup and maintenance in Osprey and customer systems, including new item implementation and customer initiatives.<\/li><li>Coordinate and support large-scale planning meetings, including JBP, ICP, industry events, and internal business planning sessions.<\/li><li>Manage automated customer reporting, retailer reset calendars, category update submissions, and related customer forms.<\/li><li>Investigate and resolve pricing discrepancies involving contracts, EDI submissions, promotional events, and customer\/system updates.<\/li><li>Manage promotional contracts, validate dates, lead times, and funding amounts, and review promotional activities with Account Managers.<\/li><li>Coordinate sample ordering and maintain sample inventory records.<br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Qualifications:<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Bachelor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s degree preferred, or 1\u00e2\u0080\u00932 years of relevant professional experience.<\/li><li>Experience in administrative, analytical, sales support, customer support, Field Sales Representative, or Customer Account Analyst roles preferred.<\/li><li>Strong organization, time management, attention to detail, and accuracy.<\/li><li>Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, with familiarity in SharePoint and collaboration tools.<\/li><li>Ability to work independently, manage multiple priorities, communicate effectively, and collaborate with cross-functional partners.<br><br><\/li><\/ul>The approximate pay range for this position is $58,000-$85,000. Please note that the pay range provided is a good faith estimate for the position at the time of posting. Final compensation may vary based on factors including but not limited to knowledge, skills and abilities as well as geographic location.<br><br>Nestl\u00c3\u00a9 offers performance-based incentives and a competitive total rewards package, which includes a 401k with company match, healthcare coverage and a broad range of other benefits. \u00e2\u0080\u00afIncentives and\/or benefit packages may vary depending on the position. Learn more at\u00e2\u0080\u00afAbout Us |\u00e2\u0080\u00afNestl\u00c3\u00a9 Careers (nestlejobs.com)<br><br>F4G: C&amp;B<br><br>It is our business imperative to remain a very inclusive workplace.<br><br>To our veterans and separated service members, you're at the forefront of our minds as we recruit top talent to join Nestl\u00c3\u00a9. The skills you've gained while serving our country, such as flexibility, agility, and leadership, are much like the skills that will make you successful in this role. In addition, with our commitment to an inclusive work environment, we recognize the exceptional engagement and innovation displayed by individuals with disabilities. Nestl\u00c3\u00a9 seeks such skilled and qualified individuals to share our mission where you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll join a cohort of others who have chosen to call Nestl\u00c3\u00a9 home.<br><br>The Nestl\u00c3\u00a9 Companies are equal employment opportunity employers. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or veteran status or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Prior to the next step in the recruiting process, we welcome you to inform us confidentially if you may require any special accommodations in order to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Contact us at accommodations@nestle.com or please dial 711 and provide this number to the operator: 1-800-321-6467.<br><br>This position is not eligible for Visa Sponsorship.<br><br>Review our applicant privacy notice before applying at https:\/\/www.nestlejobs.com\/privacy.<br><br>Job Requisition: 411945<br><br>#Salaried<br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **DILIGENT** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Seattle, ","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-customer-account-associate-albertsons-nestle-1135671","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-customer-account-associate-albertsons-nestle-1135671"},{"slug":"remote-ship-to-shore-technician-carnival-corporation-1135651","id":"1135651","epoch":1785345614,"date":"2026-07-29T17:20:14+00:00","company":"Carnival Corporation","company_logo":"","position":"Ship to Shore Technician","tags":["education","technical","customer support","exec","ops"],"description":"<strong>Job Description<br><br><\/strong>As a Ship-to-Shore Technician, you will play a vital role in supporting the safe and efficient operation of vessels arriving and departing at the port. This position involves working on the dock to ensure the proper mooring, securing, and release of ships, while maintaining safety and operational standards. In addition to mooring responsibilities, the role will also involve performing general maintenance and support tasks as required to ensure overall port and equipment readiness.<br><br>The Ship-to-Shore Technician is responsible for, but not limited to the following:<br><br><strong>Docking and Undocking Operations<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Assist in safely docking and undocking cruise ships at port using mooring lines, ropes, and related equipment. <\/li><li>Work in coordination with the ship\u00e2\u0080\u0099s captain, crew, and port authorities to ensure that vessels are safely secured and aligned with docking infrastructure. <br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Mooring Line Management:<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Handle and manage mooring lines, ensuring they are properly fastened, tense, and released. <\/li><li>Perform visual inspection of mooring lines and related equipment regularly for wear and damage, ensuring everything is in safe working condition. (Regularly performed by ship crew)<br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Ship and Dock Safety<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Maintain safety protocols during mooring procedures, ensuring that all tasks are performed in accordance with safety regulations. <\/li><li>Monitor weather conditions and report any changes that could affect docking or undocking procedures. <br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Communication and Coordination<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Communicate effectively with other team members on board and shore-based personnel. <\/li><li>Work with the Port Authorities to ensure the timely and safe transfer of passengers and cargo. <br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Emergency Procedures<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Be trained to respond in case of an emergency during docking or undocking operations, including accidents or hazardous situations. <\/li><li>Ensure all mooring operations are conducted efficiently and safely, even under adverse weather conditions or emergencies. <br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>PPE Equipment (MANDATORY)<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Must always be in possession of steel toe boots (or prescribed non-slip safety shoes), safety vest, hard hat, gloves, radio\/communication device. (To be provided by Carnival)<br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Cleaning &amp; Maintenance of Pier &amp; Mooring Equipment &amp; Fixtures: <br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Ensure all mooring equipment such as winches, ropes, and fenders are properly maintained and operational (through visual checks and inspections). <\/li><li>Gangway Inspections &amp; Maintenance: Inspect gangway components for wear, corrosion, proper tension, secure connections, and smooth operation to ensure safe pedestrian access and functionality. <\/li><li>Fenders: Conduct visual inspections of pier fenders and associated hardware to identify cracks, deformation, excessive wear, or damage caused by vessel contact, and report deficiencies as needed. <\/li><li>Mooring Bollards: Regularly inspect mooring bollards for structural integrity, including corrosion, cracks, loose anchor bolts, foundation stress, and coating condition, to ensure safe vessel mooring. <\/li><li>Stanchions &amp; Pier Fixtures: Inspect stanchions and associated components for corrosion, damage, misalignment, or instability, ensuring they remain secure and serviceable. <\/li><li>Ropes: Inspect ropes for wear, fraying, or damage, and verify they are properly positioned and suitable for continued use. <\/li><li>Mooring Equipment Maintenance: Perform minor maintenance and repairs of mooring equipment when necessary. <\/li><li>Pier &amp; Dock Cleaning: Maintain clean, safe, and non-slip pier surfaces by removing dirt, salt, algae, stains, debris and other buildup by pressure washing and using prescribed cleaning equipment and solutions, along all designated cruise pier and trestle areas. <\/li><li>Cleaning Equipment Operation: Safely inspect, operate, and maintain cleaning equipment, including scrubbers and pressure washers, ensuring proper use, cleaning, and storage after each operation. <br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Additional Maintenance Support Activities<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Perform minor maintenance support to technical teams including plumbing, electrical, masonry, carpentry, and HVAC functions. <br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Mandatory Training:<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Maintain compliance with organizational requirements by attending and participating in all required company training sessions. <br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Lagoon Care<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Perform maintenance\/inspections of lagoon systems. <br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Education:<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Education: High School Diploma. <\/li><li>Maintenance knowledge is preferred. <\/li><li>Certified Pool Operator (CPO) required within 6 months of employment start. <\/li><li>Three to Five years' experience working in a mooring or associated fields. <br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Essential Experience Required:<br><br><\/strong>Must be physically fit. Must have strong customer service skills. Ability to work in an outdoor environment. Ability to multi-task and think critically. Previous work experience preferred. Prolonged periods standing and working outside. Must be able to lift, up to 50 pounds at times. All island employees must be physically able to participate in emergency lifesaving procedures and drills. Full use\/range of motion of arms and legs as well as full visual, verbal and hearing abilities are required to receive and give instructions in the event of an emergency. Ability to read and write English to understand and interpret written procedures. This includes the ability to give and receive instructions in written and verbal forms and to effectively present information and respond to questions from guests, managers, and co-workers.<br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **UNDISPUTABLE** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"East Grand Bahama, ","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-ship-to-shore-technician-carnival-corporation-1135651","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-ship-to-shore-technician-carnival-corporation-1135651"},{"slug":"remote-care-navigator-level-1-ready-1135674","id":"1135674","epoch":1785344698,"date":"2026-07-29T17:04:58+00:00","company":"Ready","company_logo":"","position":"Care Navigator Level 1","tags":["testing","education","exec","content writing","marketing","part time","design","technical","coordinator","customer support","travel","microsoft","ops","excel","medical","digital nomad","consulting","supervisor","dev","speech","sys admin","analyst","finance","c","sales","recruiter","product manager","golang","engineer","full time","python","data annotation","linguistics","data science","junior","stats","internship","senior"],"description":"<strong>Job Type:<br><\/strong>Full-Time<br><br><strong>Location:<br><\/strong>Fully Remote (U.S.)<br><br><strong>Reports To:<br><\/strong>Care Navigator Supervisor<br><br><strong>Pay:<br><\/strong>$22.00 per hour<br><br><strong>Classification:<br><\/strong>Non-Exempt \/ Hourly<br><br>Are you a healthcare professional who thrives in a fast-paced environment and wants more than \u00e2\u0080\u009cjust a call center job\u00e2\u0080\u009d? myLaurel is hiring a Care Navigator, Level 1 to serve as the critical first connection our patients have with the myLaurel care team.<br><br>This is a specialized role for someone who wants to build foundational skills in healthcare navigation, clinical problem-solving, and cross-functional collaboration \u00e2\u0080\u0094 with real room to grow. You'll be the voice patients and caregivers turn to for scheduling, education, and support as they navigate their care journey at home.<br><br>We're looking for high-performers who are proactive, adaptable, and eager to grow within a high-impact startup environment.<br><br><strong>Key Responsibilities<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Primary Point of Contact: Serve as the lead contact for patients and caregivers via high-volume inbound and outbound calls. <\/li><li>Scheduling: Coordinate and schedule in-home and virtual care visits efficiently and accurately. <\/li><li>Patient Education: Educate patients on myLaurel program services and set clear, empathetic expectations for their care journey. <\/li><li>Post-Visit Support: Manage critical post-visit needs, including equipment coordination, pharmacy requests, and clinical documentation. <\/li><li>Systems Management: Maintain high-integrity documentation of every interaction within our internal systems and Electronic Health Record (EHR). <\/li><li>Cross-Functional Partnership: Collaborate daily with clinical and operations teams to deliver a seamless, \u00e2\u0080\u009cwhite-glove\u00e2\u0080\u009d patient experience. <br><br><br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>What You Bring<br><br><\/strong><ul><li>2+ years of professional experience in a healthcare call center or patient facing environment. <\/li><li>Proficiency with Electronic Health Record (EHR) platforms (e.g., Epic, Athena, Cerner, or similar) required. <\/li><li>A dedicated, private, HIPAA-compliant workspace with a door. <\/li><li>Reliable high-speed internet (minimum 20 Mbps download \/ 5 Mbps upload). <\/li><li>Exceptional active listening skills and the ability to multitask across multiple software systems while maintaining an empathetic phone presence. <\/li><li>High school diploma or GED required. <br><br><br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>Why Work With Us<br><br><br><\/strong><ul><li>Join a mission-driven team bringing hospital-level care into patients' homes. <\/li><li>Step onto a defined Care Navigator career path, with room to grow into senior and specialist roles. <\/li><li>Fully remote role with a supportive, collaborative team culture. <\/li><li>Be part of a high-growth startup transforming acute and transitional care for frail, elderly, and medically complex patients. <br><br><br><br><\/li><\/ul><strong>About MyLaurel<br><\/strong>myLaurel was founded on the belief that a meaningful portion of hospital care can \u00e2\u0080\u0094 and should \u00e2\u0080\u0094 be delivered in the comfort of home. As a tech-enabled medical group, we provide on-demand acute and transitional care to frail, elderly, or medically complex patients at home, helping them avoid the traditional pathway of ambulance, emergency department, hospital admission, and post-acute facility care.<br><br>For high-risk populations, myLaurel achieves 33% lower ED utilization, a 49% absolute reduction in readmissions, and a Net Promoter Score of 97. myLaurel has been named to Fast Company's Most Innovative Companies and the New York Digital Health 100. Learn more at mylaurelhealth.com.<br><br>We may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses and identifying potential inconsistencies or verification signals in application materials based on available information. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.<br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **CONGRATULATORY** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Seattle, Seattle, Washington, United States","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-care-navigator-level-1-ready-1135674","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-care-navigator-level-1-ready-1135674"},{"slug":"remote-fde-lead-wipro-1135645","id":"1135645","epoch":1785340857,"date":"2026-07-29T16:00:57+00:00","company":"Wipro","company_logo":"","position":"FDE Lead","tags":["technical","design","exec","digital nomad"],"description":"Job description:<br><br>Job Description \u00cd\u008f \u00cd\u008f \u00cd\u008f \u00cd\u008f <p>Reinvent your world.\u00e2\u0080\u00afWe are building a modern Wipro. We are an end-to-end digital transformation partner with the boldest ambitions. To realize them, we need people inspired by reinvention. Of yourself, your career, and your skills. We want to see the constant evolution of our business and our industry. It has always been in our DNA - as the world around us changes, so do we. Join a business powered by purpose and a place that empowers you to design your own reinvention. Come to Wipro. Realize your ambitions.\u00c2\u00a0<\/p><p>Applications from people with disabilities are explicitly welcome.\u00c2\u00a0<\/p><br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **AMITY** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Bengaluru, ","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-fde-lead-wipro-1135645","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-fde-lead-wipro-1135645"},{"slug":"remote-legal-expert-weekday-ai-1135616","id":"1135616","epoch":1785340816,"date":"2026-07-29T16:00:16+00:00","company":"Weekday AI","company_logo":"","position":"Legal Expert","tags":["education","customer support","content writing","legal","sys admin","part time","non tech"],"description":"<p>This role is for one of our clients<\/p><p>Compensation: $65 - $90 per hour<\/p><p><\/p><p>Join an innovative AI initiative dedicated to improving how advanced AI systems understand, interpret, and reason about legal concepts. We are seeking experienced legal professionals to contribute their real-world expertise by evaluating AI-generated content, providing subject-matter guidance, and helping develop more accurate and reliable AI solutions for legal applications.<\/p><p>This is a flexible, fully remote, part-time opportunity requiring approximately 10 hours per week, with the potential for continued engagement based on project needs and performance.<\/p>\nKey Responsibilities<ul><li>Review and evaluate AI-generated legal content, written materials, and responses for accuracy, completeness, and quality.<\/li><li>Answer legal questions and provide clear, well-reasoned feedback based on your professional expertise and practical experience.<\/li><li>Identify and recommend authoritative legal references, research materials, and resources relevant to your area of practice.<\/li><li>Share insights into real-world legal workflows, professional standards, research methods, and day-to-day legal practice.<\/li><li>Collaborate with a multidisciplinary team of subject matter experts to improve AI performance across a variety of legal domains.<\/li><li>Help ensure AI-generated legal outputs align with professional standards, sound legal reasoning, and practical application.<\/li><\/ul>Required Qualifications<ul><li>Active admission to at least one United States State Bar.<\/li><li>Minimum 2 years of professional legal experience, preferably across multiple practice areas such as contracts, litigation, corporate law, intellectual property, or regulatory and compliance.<\/li><li>Strong proficiency in legal research using standard legal resources, including case law databases, statutes, regulations, and legal treatises.<\/li><li>Excellent written communication skills with the ability to explain complex legal concepts clearly and accurately.<\/li><li>Experience creating legal content such as briefs, memoranda, legal opinions, CLE materials, or similar documentation is a plus.<\/li><li>Comfortable using AI-powered tools such as ChatGPT or similar platforms.<\/li><li>Based in the United States.<\/li><li>Professional proficiency in English.<\/li><li>Ability to commit approximately 10 hours per week on a consistent basis.<\/li><\/ul>Preferred Qualifications<ul><li>Background as a legal librarian or experience supporting legal research.<\/li><li>Experience mentoring, training, or reviewing legal work.<\/li><li>Interest in the intersection of law, technology, and artificial intelligence.<\/li><\/ul>Why Join<ul><li>Help shape the future of AI-powered legal technology.<\/li><li>Apply your legal expertise to improve the quality, accuracy, and reliability of AI-generated legal content.<\/li><li>Collaborate with researchers, engineers, and fellow legal professionals on impactful AI initiatives.<\/li><li>Enjoy the flexibility of a fully remote, part-time engagement with opportunities for ongoing collaboration.<\/li><\/ul>Equal Opportunity<p>We are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace and welcome qualified applicants from all backgrounds. Reasonable accommodations are available throughout the application and engagement process.<\/p>Contract &amp; Engagement Details<ul><li>Independent contractor engagement.<\/li><li>Fully remote with flexible working hours.<\/li><li>Project duration may vary based on business needs and individual performance.<\/li><li>Work does not require access to confidential or proprietary information from any current or former employer.<\/li><li>Payments are issued weekly based on approved work completed.<\/li><li>At this time, we are unable to support H1-B or STEM OPT candidates.<\/li><\/ul><br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **PREFERS** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-legal-expert-weekday-ai-1135616","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-legal-expert-weekday-ai-1135616"},{"slug":"remote-political-powerplay-1135622","id":"1135622","epoch":1785340187,"date":"2026-07-29T15:49:47+00:00","company":"PowerPlay","company_logo":"","position":"Political","tags":["project manager","exec"],"description":"Precision, scale, and measurable impact for modern political campaigns. PowerPlay brings broadcast-level credibility to the digital space with transparent reporting, brand-safe environments, and proven performance.<br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **HEROIC** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Naobaricha, ","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-political-powerplay-1135622","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-political-powerplay-1135622"},{"slug":"remote-sports-powerplay-1135786","id":"1135786","epoch":1785340180,"date":"2026-07-29T15:49:40+00:00","company":"PowerPlay","company_logo":"","position":"Sports","tags":["ads"],"description":"Reach passionate sports audiences with premium, non-skippable ads during live streaming events and through exclusive national syndication with Boomer Esiason.<br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **EXALTATION** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Sports Park, ","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-sports-powerplay-1135786","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-sports-powerplay-1135786"},{"slug":"remote-program-amp-events-coordinator-lsp-association-1135669","id":"1135669","epoch":1785339099,"date":"2026-07-29T15:31:39+00:00","company":"LSP Association","company_logo":"","position":"Program &amp; Events Coordinator","tags":["testing","education","exec","content writing","marketing","part time","design","technical","coordinator","customer support","travel","microsoft","ops","excel","medical","digital nomad"],"description":"<p><strong>About the LSPA: <\/strong>The LSP Association (LSPA) is a non-profit association for Massachusetts Licensed Site Professionals (LSPs) and other related environmental practitioners who work on behalf of property owners, operators, and other involved parties to assess and cleanup oil and hazardous materials (OHM) released to the environment. LSPs are licensed by the Commonwealth to oversee this work and, since 1993, over 40,000 contaminated properties have been brought into regulatory compliance. <\/p><p><br><\/p><p>The LSPA's mission is to support our membership in achieving and maintaining a high standard of practice in the assessment and remediation of contaminated sites in Massachusetts and New England. The LSPA provides technical and educational resources to our membership in the form of programming, networking events, committees, and resources. The LSPA also serves as an advocate to the profession with MassDEP, the LSP Board of Registration, and the state legislature, and as a resource to the public.<\/p><p><br><\/p><p><strong>Job Description: <\/strong>The Program &amp; Events Coordinator plays a critical role in the success of the LSPA and serves as a primary point of contact for our members, volunteers, and sponsors. This individual is responsible for planning, coordinating, and executing the association's educational programs and networking events, administering the sponsorship program, and providing customer service support. Success in this position means delivering high-quality member experiences, maintaining strong relationships with volunteers and sponsors, and ensuring the smooth administration of our continuing education program.<\/p><p><br><\/p><p>The ideal candidate is highly organized, detail-oriented, customer-focused, and comfortable managing multiple projects simultaneously. This individual enjoys working independently while collaborating closely with volunteers, board members, speakers, sponsors, and staff.<\/p><p><br><\/p><p><strong>Key Responsibilities: <\/strong><\/p><ul><li><strong>Educational Programs<\/strong>: Coordinate, plan, and manage programs and speakers for all LSPA courses, membership meetings, emerging professional events, the Annual Fall Party, and the Environmental Symposium. The LSPA hosts one to three events per month with 25-250 people in attendance. Approximately 65% of programming is hosted virtually. Content creation is performed in conjunction with input from the Executive Director, Committee Chairs, Education Committee, and Board of Directors. <\/li><li><strong>Event Logistics: <\/strong>For in-person events, source event venues and help facilitate contracts; plan food and beverage, room set-up, and audiovisual needs; reconcile venue bills; and serve as the point of contact on-site. For virtual programs, setup and run the virtual meeting platform, monitor attendance and engagement, create moderator scripts and slides, and train speakers on how to use the virtual platform.<\/li><li><strong>Continuing Education (CE) Administration<\/strong>: Compile CE materials for all educational courses and meetings; submit materials for credit approval with the LSP Board of Registration, the Connecticut Licensed Environmental Professional (LEP) Board, and other Boards\/entities; maintain CE records related to attendance, engagement, and evaluation; issue certificates of attendance to attendees; and attend monthly virtual LSP Board of Registration meetings.<\/li><li><strong>Sponsorship<\/strong>: Help administer the corporate and event sponsorship program, including updating the sponsorship prospectus, facilitating invoices\/payments, maintaining contact lists, conducting outreach, and working with sponsors to access their sponsorship benefits.<\/li><li><strong>Member Service and Organizational Support<\/strong>: Help monitor and respond to inquiries received through the organization email inbox; provide customer service to members, sponsors, speakers, and event attendees; attend Board meetings, leadership meetings, and committee meetings as requested; and support association operations and special projects as needed.<\/li><\/ul><p><br><\/p><p><strong>Qualifications<\/strong><\/p><p>The person hired for this role should have the following qualifications:<\/p><p><br><\/p><p><strong>Experience:<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>2-5 years of experience in program\/event planning, project management, or another related field.<\/li><li>Excellent written and verbal communication skills, and proven ability to provide excellent customer service.<\/li><li>Strong project management skills with excellent attention to detail.<\/li><li>Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines independently.<\/li><li>Comfortable coordinating, building relationships with, and communicating professionally with members, volunteers, sponsors, vendors, and other external stakeholders\/partners.<\/li><\/ul><p><br><\/p><p><strong>Technology:<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Microsoft 365 (Outlook, Teams, SharePoint, Word, Excel, PowerPoint).<\/li><li>Zoom Meetings and Zoom Webinar, including coordinating presenters from multiple locations, incorporating polling, and managing technical issues.<\/li><li>Association management systems (AMS) or member databases.<\/li><li>Online registration and evaluation platforms.<\/li><li>Canva or similar design tools (preferred, not required).<\/li><\/ul><p> <\/p><p><strong>Preferred Qualifications (not required):<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Experience working for a nonprofit organization, professional association, or membership-based organization.<\/li><li>Experience with the environmental sciences industry.<\/li><li>Familiarity with sponsorship development or relationship management.<\/li><li>Bachelor's degree, Associate's degree with relevant experience, or significant relevant professional experience demonstrating the knowledge, skills, and abilities required to perform the position successfully.<\/li><\/ul><p> <\/p><p> <strong>Why Join the LSPA?<\/strong><\/p><p>This is an opportunity to work with a respected association that supports environmental professionals making a meaningful impact on public health and environmental protection throughout Massachusetts and New England. As a small organization, we offer autonomy, flexibility, and the opportunity to build relationships with industry leaders while helping shape the educational and professional development experiences of our members. Compensation and benefits include:<\/p><ul><li><strong>Salary<\/strong>: The salary range for this position is $70,000\u00e2\u0080\u0093$80,000 annually. Compensation will be based on a variety of factors such as individual qualifications and experience.<\/li><li><strong>Benefits<\/strong>: LSPA employees receive $300 per month for a Healthcare Reimbursement Account (HRA) that may be used to reimburse certain medical and insurance-related expenses. The organization does not currently offer group health or dental insurance plans. In addition, employees have access to a 401(k) plan. <\/li><li><strong>PTO<\/strong>: 15 days of paid time off (PTO) annually for the first three years (increases to 20 days thereafter). The LSPA also provides 14 holidays per year (inclusive of 5 floating holidays).<\/li><li><strong>Fully remote position<\/strong>: Candidates may reside anywhere in New England, with preference given to Massachusetts-based applicants. Travel to Massachusetts-based programs and events approximately 10\u00e2\u0080\u009312 times annually is required.<\/li><li><strong>Reimbursement for home office expenses<\/strong>: $750 annually.<\/li><\/ul><p><br><\/p><p><strong>How to Apply<\/strong><\/p><p>Please submit a cover letter and resume to mmorris@lspa.org. Applications without cover letters or that request compensation\/benefits beyond what we can provide will not be reviewed. <\/p><p><br><\/p><p><em>The LSPA is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. If you need a reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, contact mmorris@lspa.org.<\/em><\/p><p><br><\/p><p><em>The LSPA is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All employment decisions are based on business needs, job requirements, and individual qualifications, without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran, or disability status.<\/em><\/p><br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **PEACEFUL** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Massachusetts, Massachusetts, United States","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-program-amp-events-coordinator-lsp-association-1135669","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-program-amp-events-coordinator-lsp-association-1135669"},{"slug":"remote-us-tax-preparer-ambit-tax-and-accounting-1135646","id":"1135646","epoch":1785338570,"date":"2026-07-29T15:22:50+00:00","company":"Ambit Tax and Accounting","company_logo":"","position":"US Tax Preparer","tags":["technical","design","exec","digital nomad","accounting","dev"],"description":"<p><strong><u>US Tax Manager<\/u><\/strong><\/p><p>The ideal candidate should be an <strong>Enrolled Agent and <\/strong>will be responsible for US Tax Return Preparation &amp; Review in coordination with the CPA Firms. <strong>Do not apply if no US Tax Return Experience. This will be client facing role so fluency in English is a must.<\/strong><\/p><p><br><\/p><p><strong><u>Responsibilities<\/u><\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Preparation, review and filing of Individual, Partnership and S-Corp. Federal and State returns<\/li><li>Preparation, review and filing of Corporate Federal and State returns<\/li><li>Doing a detailed research with regards to Federal income Tax.<\/li><li>Response to the notices issued by IRS and State Tax authority with regard to Income Tax.<\/li><li>Direct communication with US CPA on a regular basis.<\/li><li>Should have worked on 1040, 1065,1120,1120s and 990. <\/li><li>Adherence to deadlines and an attitude to meet them are a must for this job.<\/li><li>The ability to work in a team and take up responsibility for the work done will be a crucial aspect for the candidate.<\/li><li>Very strong Command on English is a must.<\/li><\/ul><p><br><\/p><p><strong>Qualifications<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Minimum 3-5 years experience in US Tax return preparation &amp; review.<\/li><li><strong>Enrolled Agent License is a must.<\/strong><\/li><li>Must be ready to work in US Time Zone (Night Shift).<\/li><li>Strong verbal or written communication skills.<\/li><li>Strong knowledge on Software like Drake, Ultratax, Proseries, Turbotax etc.<\/li><\/ul><p><br><\/p><p><strong><u>Salary<\/u><\/strong><\/p><p>Salary is not a constraint for the right candidate.<\/p><br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **AFFORD** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Vijayawada, ","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-us-tax-preparer-ambit-tax-and-accounting-1135646","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-us-tax-preparer-ambit-tax-and-accounting-1135646"},{"slug":"remote-estimator-key-talent-solutions-1135773","id":"1135773","epoch":1785338428,"date":"2026-07-29T15:20:28+00:00","company":"Key Talent Solutions","company_logo":"","position":"Estimator","tags":["sys admin","exec","finance","scheme","excel","sales","engineer","recruiter","education","ops","customer support","infosec","travel","medical","game dev","c","legal","accounting"],"description":"<p>The ideal candidate will be responsible for appropriately evaluating the cost of a project, and evaluating the cost to take on that project. The candidate will be familiar with our competitive advantages as an organization and will be able to communicate those to our benefit throughout the bidding process.<\/p><p><br><\/p><p><strong>Responsibilities<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Maintain knowledge of competitive advantages in the industry to aid bidding process<\/li><li>Resolve cost discrepancies by collecting and analyzing information<\/li><li>Obtain accurate quotes for materials and systems to establish accurate cost estimates<\/li><\/ul><p><br><\/p><p><strong>Qualifications<\/strong><\/p><p><br><\/p><ul><li>Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance or equivalent experience<\/li><li>Solid understanding of basic accounting principles<\/li><li>Familiarity with blueprints and ability to read plans<\/li><li>1 - 3 years' of construction experience preferred<\/li><\/ul><p><br><\/p><br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **EVENTFUL** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Exeter, ","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-estimator-key-talent-solutions-1135773","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-estimator-key-talent-solutions-1135773"},{"slug":"remote-lean-practitioner-kaizenworldai-1135629","id":"1135629","epoch":1785337830,"date":"2026-07-29T15:10:30+00:00","company":"KaizenworldAI","company_logo":"","position":"Lean Practitioner","tags":["infosec","javascript"],"description":"au.seek.com<br><br>Performing security verification<br><br>This website uses a security service to protect against malicious bots. This page is displayed while the website verifies you are not a bot.<br><br>Verification successful. Waiting for au.seek.com to respond<br><br>Enable JavaScript and cookies to continue<br\/><br\/>Please mention the word **WILLINGNESS** and tag RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMjYwMToyODA6NTI4MTpkNzUwOmU5YTQ6YjViMTpmZDQwOjUzY2M=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.","location":"Sydney, ","apply_url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-lean-practitioner-kaizenworldai-1135629","salary_min":0,"salary_max":0,"logo":"","url":"https:\/\/remoteOK.com\/remote-jobs\/remote-lean-practitioner-kaizenworldai-1135629"},{"slug":"remote-continuous-improvement-lead-kaizenworldai-1135630","id":"1135630","epoch":1785337756,"date":"2026-07-29T15:09:16+00:00","company":"KaizenworldAI","company_logo":"","position":"Continuous Improvement Lead","tags":["infosec","javascript","exec"],"description":"au.seek.com<br><br>Performing security verification<br><br>This website uses a security service to protect against malicious bots. This page is displayed while the website verifies you are